@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Code Review — /refunds listing screen
+
+**Files reviewed:**
+- `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx`
+- `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx`
+- `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/refunds.pt.json`
+
+**Playbooks consulted:**
+- `packages/app/react/CLAUDE.md` (state-placement five questions, enum-label catalog vs. icon/color/variant maps, dialog store)
+- `.claude/skills/route/react/registry.yaml` (bp-02 through bp-13, RTE-02, RTE-04)
+- `.claude/skills/component/react/registry.yaml` (bp-01, bp-03, bp-06, bp-12, bp-14, bp-17, bp-20, CMP-02, CMP-P05, CMP-P17)
+- `.claude/skills/review/SKILL.md` (finding format)
+
+---
+
+## Status: CHANGES_REQUESTED
+
+---
+
+## Bad Practices Found
+
+### Blockers
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:37-44` ↔ `…/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:58-67`
+  - Practice: route `bp-02`, route `bp-13`, component `bp-01`, component `bp-12`
+  - Why bad: The route shell calls `useListOrders` and passes `data`, `search`, and `onSearchParamsChange` down as props to `RefundTableSection`. This is the container anti-pattern: the route becomes a data orchestrator rather than a thin URL shell. The component cannot be mounted independently, React Query deduplication is bypassed, and the navigation callback is prop-drilled instead of the component owning its own `routeApi.useNavigate()`. The `_navigate` stub in the component (line 69) confirms the author knew this and left it half-done. The hardcoded `isLoading={false}` at line 126 is a direct symptom — the component has no access to the query's real `isPending` flag because it never calls the hook.
+  - Required refactor:
+    - **Route `index.tsx`**: Remove the `useListOrders` call, the `search` binding, and the `navigate` binding. Render `<RefundTableSection />` with zero props.
+    - **Component**: Delete the `RefundTableSectionProps` interface and its three prop fields (`data`, `search`, `onSearchParamsChange`). Add `const search = routeApi.useSearch()`, `const navigate = routeApi.useNavigate()`, and `const { data, isPending } = useListOrders({ page: search.page, limit: search.limit })` inside the component body. Replace `handleNextPage` + `onSearchParamsChange({ page: … })` with `navigate({ search: prev => ({ ...prev, page: prev.page + 1 }) })`. Pass `isLoading={isPending}` (not `false`) to `DataTable`.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:17`
+  - Practice: route `bp-04`
+  - Why bad: `.extend()` overwrites SDK field definitions wholesale — their validators, coercions, and defaults are silently replaced. The search schema no longer inherits the SDK's constraints for `page`, `limit`, etc., which can allow invalid inputs to reach the API and makes the schema diverge from the single source of truth.
+  - Required refactor: `const refundsSearchSchema = listOrdersQueryParamsSchema.and(z.object({ selectedRefundId: z.string().optional() }))`
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:25-28`
+  - Practice: route `bp-05`
+  - Why bad: Without `errorComponent`, any unhandled throw inside the route subtree (network error, SDK validation failure) crashes the entire app tree up to the nearest React error boundary instead of rendering a scoped, recoverable error UI.
+  - Required refactor: Add `import { RouteError } from '@/components/RouteError'` and add `errorComponent: RouteError,` inside the `createFileRoute(…)({…})` options.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:8, 109`
+  - Practice: component `bp-03`, `CMP-02`
+  - Why bad: `import { Trash } from 'lucide-react'` mixes a second icon library into the bundle. The only sanctioned icon set is `@tabler/icons-react`. Two libraries means two icon grids, visual inconsistency, and unnecessary bundle weight.
+  - Required refactor: Replace `import { Trash } from 'lucide-react'` with `import { IconTrash } from '@tabler/icons-react'` and update line 109 `<Trash />` → `<IconTrash />`.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:48`
+  - Practice: component `bp-14`
+  - Why bad: `order.status === 'REFUNDED'` is a bare string literal comparison. TypeScript cannot flag this if `PaymentStatusEnum.REFUNDED` is later renamed or if the field type narrows differently. Exhaustiveness and rename-safety are lost.
+  - Required refactor: `const isRefunded = order.status === PaymentStatusEnum.REFUNDED` — `PaymentStatusEnum` is already imported on line 5.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:105`
+  - Practice: component `bp-17`, `CMP-P17`
+  - Why bad: `<Button size="icon" onClick={…}><IconSend /></Button>` has no `aria-label`. Screen readers announce it as an unlabeled control; this fails WCAG 2.1 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value). Note: the `<Trash />` button on line 109 correctly has `aria-label` — only this one is missing.
+  - Required refactor: Add `aria-label={t('refunds.exportAction')}` (or an appropriate action label), add the key to `refunds.pt.json` and the matching `en.json` entry.
+
+### Majors
+
+- [ ] **[Major]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:25-28`
+  - Practice: `Skill:route:RTE-02`
+  - Why bad: Top-level page routes must declare `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Label' }`. Without it the breadcrumb trail is empty/broken for the `/refunds` page and the app layout has no label to display for this route.
+  - Required refactor: Add `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Reembolsos' },` to the `createFileRoute(…)({…})` options.
+
+- [ ] **[Major]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:53`
+  - Practice: component `bp-06`
+  - Why bad: `bg-blue-500 text-white` are raw Tailwind color-scale classes, not design tokens. They will not respond to dark mode, theming, or the design system's semantic color palette.
+  - Required refactor: Replace the hardcoded `<span className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-1 text-white">↺</span>` with a semantic `<Badge variant="info">↺</Badge>` (or whichever variant conveys "refunded" in the design system).
+
+### Minors
+
+- [ ] **[Minor]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:67`
+  - Practice: component `bp-20`
+  - Why bad: `RefundTableSection` renders a `<div>` root but its props interface does not extend `ComponentProps<'div'>`. Callers cannot pass `className` to adjust layout, which is the standard composition contract for section-level components.
+  - Required refactor: Change the signature to `export function RefundTableSection({ className, ...props }: ComponentProps<'div'>)` and merge: `<div className={cn('flex flex-col gap-4', className)} {...props}>`. (This naturally follows from fixing bp-01/bp-12 since the props interface is being rewritten anyway.)
+
+---
+
+## Refactor Actions Required
+
+1. **(bp-02 / bp-13 / bp-01 / bp-12)** Strip `useListOrders`, `search`, and `navigate` from the route shell; let `RefundTableSection` own the query via `routeApi.useSearch()` + `useListOrders` + `routeApi.useNavigate()`.
+2. **(bp-04)** Change `.extend({…})` → `.and(z.object({…}))` on the search schema.
+3. **(bp-05)** Add `errorComponent: RouteError` to the Route options.
+4. **(RTE-02)** Add `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Reembolsos' }` to the Route options.
+5. **(bp-03 / CMP-02)** Replace `lucide-react` `Trash` with `@tabler/icons-react` `IconTrash`.
+6. **(bp-14)** Change `=== 'REFUNDED'` → `=== PaymentStatusEnum.REFUNDED`.
+7. **(bp-06)** Replace `bg-blue-500 text-white` span with a semantic `<Badge>` variant.
+8. **(bp-17 / CMP-P17)** Add `aria-label` to the unlabelled icon-only `<Button>` at line 105.
+9. **(bp-20)** Extend `ComponentProps<'div'>` in `RefundTableSection` and merge `className`.
+
+---
+
+## New Bad Practices Added
+
+None — all findings map to existing registry entries.
+
+---
+
+## Architecture Ambiguities
+
+None.
+
+---
+
+## Cleared (looks-wrong-but-fine)
+
+1. **`const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false)` (RefundTableSection:74)** — This is a private, transient UI disclosure flag for a popover hint panel. It does not represent server data, bookmarkable view state, cross-component shared state, or form fields. It is exactly the one sanctioned `useState` under state-placement case 5 ("truly local transient UI"). NOT a violation.
+
+2. **`REFUND_STATUS_BADGE: Record<PaymentStatus, BadgeSpec>` (RefundTableSection:30-39)** — Superficially resembles the banned `Record<Enum, string>` label map (bp-23). It is NOT: the `label` values are i18n key strings (`'enums.PaymentStatus.PAID'`), not display strings, and the `variant` values are Badge style tokens. This is the canonical enum-keyed color/variant dispatch map colocated with the owning component, as sanctioned by CLAUDE.md ("Icon/color/variant maps are a different thing — they resolve to STYLES, not labels, and they're canon"). bp-23 is NOT triggered.
+
+3. **`function StatusCell({ order }: { order: RefundItem })` (RefundTableSection:44)** — Receives a single `RefundItem` via prop because it is rendered N times inside DataTable column definitions (a `.map()`-equivalent). CMP-P05 requires exactly this: the parent owns the list query, the leaf renders one item and does not re-fetch. This is not prop-drilling. NOT a violation.
+
+4. **`refunds.pt.json` — Accented Portuguese copy** — All human-readable copy lives in the i18n JSON catalog, which is the correct and only sanctioned location. There are no inline label strings in component code. NOT a violation.
+
+---
+
+## Coverage
+
+- Files reviewed: `index.tsx` (route), `RefundTableSection/index.tsx` (component), `refunds.pt.json` (i18n)
+- Layers traced: route → component → SDK hook (read-side only; no mutations in this PR)
+- Bad practices flagged: bp-02, bp-13 (route); bp-04 (route); bp-05 (route); RTE-02 (route pattern); bp-01, bp-12, bp-03, bp-06, bp-14, bp-17, bp-20 (component)
+- Traps cleared: `useState` local disclosure, `Record<Enum,BadgeSpec>` style map, leaf-prop CMP-P05, i18n catalog copy
