+# PR Review — /refunds listing screen
+
+Playbooks read: `packages/app/react/CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills/route/react/registry.yaml`, `.claude/skills/component/react/registry.yaml`, `.claude/skills/review/SKILL.md`.
+
+---
+
+## Status: CHANGES_REQUESTED
+
+---
+
+## Bad Practices Found
+
+### Blockers
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:17`
+  - Practice: **bp-04 (route)**
+  - Why bad: `.extend()` on a Zod schema mutates/overwrites the SDK field definitions instead of intersecting with them. If the SDK schema gains stricter constraints on an existing field, `.extend()` silently replaces them — the app's search schema then diverges from the wire contract.
+  - Required refactor:
+    ```ts
+    const refundsSearchSchema = listOrdersQueryParamsSchema.and(
+      z.object({ selectedRefundId: z.string().optional() }),
+    )
+    ```
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:37,41-45`
+  - Practice: **bp-02 (route) + bp-13 (route)**
+  - Why bad: The route shell calls `useListOrders` and prop-drills `data`, `search`, and `onSearchParamsChange` into `RefundTableSection`. This is the container anti-pattern: route state is coupled to the component's shape, preventing independent component evolution, breaking React Query deduplication benefits, and making the section untestable in isolation.
+  - Required refactor: Delete the `useListOrders` call and the `const search`/`const navigate` calls from `RouteComponent`. Drop all three props from the `<RefundTableSection>` call site. The route must become a thin shell:
+    ```tsx
+    function RouteComponent() {
+      return (
+        <div className="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-6 overflow-y-auto p-6 md:p-8">
+          <RefundTableSection />
+        </div>
+      )
+    }
+    ```
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:44`
+  - Practice: **bp-10 (route)**
+  - Why bad: `onSearchParamsChange` is a callback prop threading the route's navigation function into the component. Components must navigate directly via `routeApi.useNavigate()` — passing the callback inverts the ownership boundary and makes the route responsible for how the component updates search params.
+  - Required refactor: Removed as part of bp-02 fix above. Inside `RefundTableSection`, call `routeApi.useNavigate()` directly.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:25-28`
+  - Practice: **bp-05 (route)**
+  - Why bad: No `errorComponent` is registered. If `validateSearch` throws (malformed deep-link) or a loader rejects, TanStack Router surfaces a blank screen with no recovery UI.
+  - Required refactor:
+    ```tsx
+    import { RouteError } from '@/components/RouteError'
+
+    export const Route = createFileRoute('/(app)/refunds/')({
+      staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Reembolsos' },
+      validateSearch: zodValidator(refundsSearchSchema),
+      errorComponent: RouteError,
+      component: RouteComponent,
+    })
+    ```
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:8`
+  - Practice: **bp-03 (component)**
+  - Why bad: `Trash` is imported from `lucide-react`. The project's only sanctioned icon library is `@tabler/icons-react`. Mixing libraries increases bundle size, breaks visual consistency, and triggers the mechanical `lucide-react` detector.
+  - Required refactor:
+    ```ts
+    import { IconTrash } from '@tabler/icons-react'
+    ```
+    Replace `<Trash />` at line 110 with `<IconTrash />`.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:48`
+  - Practice: **bp-14 (component)**
+  - Why bad: `order.status === 'REFUNDED'` compares against a raw string literal. If the SDK enum value is ever renamed the comparison silently always-fails. The enum constant is already imported (`PaymentStatusEnum`).
+  - Required refactor:
+    ```ts
+    const isRefunded = order.status === PaymentStatusEnum.REFUNDED
+    ```
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:105-107`
+  - Practice: **bp-17 (component)**
+  - Why bad: `<Button size="icon" onClick={...}><IconSend /></Button>` has no `aria-label`. Icon-only buttons are invisible to screen readers and automated accessibility audits. (The delete button at line 109 is correctly labelled — only this one is missing it.)
+  - Required refactor:
+    ```tsx
+    <Button size="icon" aria-label={t('refunds.exportMenu')} onClick={() => setMenuOpen(o => !o)}>
+      <IconSend />
+    </Button>
+    ```
+    Add the corresponding key to `refunds.pt.json` and the English locale file.
+
+- [ ] **[Blocker]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:58-65,67`
+  - Practice: **bp-01 (component) + bp-12 (component)**
+  - Why bad: `RefundTableSectionProps` declares `data: ListOrders200 | undefined`, `search: { page, limit, selectedRefundId? }`, and `onSearchParamsChange` as props. The component must own its data query and read search state from the route API directly — receiving these as props is the same container anti-pattern as route bp-02 from the component's side. `onSearchParamsChange` specifically is the mechanical detector for bp-12.
+  - Required refactor: Delete `RefundTableSectionProps` entirely. Inside `RefundTableSection`:
+    ```ts
+    const search = routeApi.useSearch()
+    const navigate = routeApi.useNavigate()
+    const { data } = useListOrders({ page: search.page, limit: search.limit })
+    ```
+    Navigate for pagination directly: `navigate({ search: prev => ({ ...prev, page: search.page + 1 }) })`.
+
+### Major
+
+- [ ] **[Major]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx:53`
+  - Practice: **bp-06 (component)**
+  - Why bad: `bg-blue-500` is a raw Tailwind color-scale class. The project uses design tokens (`bg-primary`, `bg-success`, semantic variants) so that theme changes apply globally. A hardcoded scale value is invisible to the token system.
+  - Required refactor: Use a semantic token or a `Badge` variant instead of the inline `<span>`:
+    ```tsx
+    {isRefunded ? <Badge variant="secondary">↺</Badge> : null}
+    ```
+    Or whichever token variant matches the intended meaning.
+
+### Minor
+
+- [ ] **[Minor]** `packages/app/react/src/routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx:25-28`
+  - Practice: **Skill:route:RTE-02**
+  - Why bad: Page routes (non-layout) must declare `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Label' }` so the `<Header>` breadcrumb trail renders correctly. The refunds route is a top-level page and the field is absent.
+  - Required refactor: Add `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Reembolsos' }` to the route definition (shown in the bp-05 fix above).
+
+---
+
+## Refactor Actions Required
+
+1. **(bp-04)** Replace `.extend({...})` with `.and(z.object({...}))` at `index.tsx:17`.
+2. **(bp-02 + bp-13)** Strip `useListOrders`, `useSearch`, and `useNavigate` from `RouteComponent`; render `<RefundTableSection />` with no props.
+3. **(bp-10)** Removed by action 2; add `routeApi.useNavigate()` inside the component.
+4. **(bp-05 + RTE-02)** Add `errorComponent: RouteError` and `staticData: { breadcrumb: 'Reembolsos' }` to the route definition.
+5. **(bp-03)** Replace `import { Trash } from 'lucide-react'` with `import { IconTrash } from '@tabler/icons-react'`; update JSX.
+6. **(bp-14)** Change `order.status === 'REFUNDED'` → `order.status === PaymentStatusEnum.REFUNDED`.
+7. **(bp-06)** Replace `<span className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-1 text-white">↺</span>` with a token-based `Badge` or semantic className.
+8. **(bp-17)** Add `aria-label={t('refunds.exportMenu')}` to the `<IconSend>` button; add locale key to both JSON files.
+9. **(bp-01 + bp-12)** Delete `RefundTableSectionProps`; move `useListOrders` call + search reads + navigation into the component body using `routeApi.useSearch()` / `routeApi.useNavigate()`.
+
+---
+
+## New Bad Practices Added
+
+None — every finding maps to an existing registry entry.
+
+---
+
+## Architecture Ambiguities
+
+None.
+
+---
+
+## Cleared (looks-wrong-but-fine)
+
+- **`const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false)` (component:74)** — Local transient disclosure flag (popover open/closed). This is state-placement case 5 ("Truly local transient UI") from `CLAUDE.md`. It is not server data, not bookmarkable, and not shared across components. The one sanctioned `useState`. **NOT a violation.**
+
+- **`const REFUND_STATUS_BADGE: Record<PaymentStatus, BadgeSpec>` (component:30-39)** — This is a color/variant dispatch map, not a label map. The `label` values are i18n catalog keys (`'enums.PaymentStatus.PAID'`), not inline display strings. `CLAUDE.md` explicitly canonizes: "Icon/color/variant maps … resolve to STYLES … and they're canon." The bp-23 detector (`Record<…Enum…, string>`) does not match here because the value type is `BadgeSpec`, not `string`. **NOT a violation.**
+
+- **`function StatusCell({ order }: { order: RefundItem })` (component:44)** — A leaf component rendered once per row via the DataTable column cell renderer. CMP-P05 explicitly requires leaf components rendered N times in a `.map()` (or equivalent iteration) to receive their single item as a prop from the parent that owns the list. The parent (`RefundTableSection`) would own the query; `StatusCell` renders one item. **NOT a violation.**
+
+- **Accented Portuguese copy in `refunds.pt.json`** — All human-readable copy must live in the i18n JSON catalog, never as inline strings in `.tsx` files. This is exactly the right location. **NOT a violation.**
+
+---
+
+## Coverage
+
+- Files reviewed: `routes/(app)/refunds/index.tsx`, `routes/(app)/refunds/-components/RefundTableSection/index.tsx`, `routes/(app)/refunds/refunds.pt.json`
+- Layers traced: route (thin shell), component (data ownership, search state, icon/aria, enum guards), i18n catalog
+- Bad practices checked against: route registry bp-01 → bp-13, component registry bp-01 → bp-28, patterns RTE-01 → RTE-14, CMP-01 → CMP-P18
+- Query paths traced: `useListOrders` called in route shell (violation) — must move to component
+- Mutation paths traced: none in this diff
